    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0715" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.19 L 22/957</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Panaman Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lefevre</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic">February 16,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note D–No. 67 of February 8, 1921, in which, under instructions from
                    your Government and on the ground that the Government of the <pb facs="0716"
                        n="620" xml:id="pg620"/> United States has recently taken over private
                    property on Taboga Island and in Las Minas Bay, Province of Colon, you make
                    application for the reestablishment of the Mixed Claims Commission referred to
                    in Articles VI and XV of the Treaty of 1903.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to advise you that the matter has been taken up with the
                    appropriate branch of this Government and will be given due consideration, after
                    which the Department will take pleasure in advising you further.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman
                            H. Davis</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Under
                    Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
